    <statement><p>Find the equation for the
line tangent to the parametric curve:</p>
<p><me>\begin{array}{r@{\,}c@{\,}l}
x \amp  = \amp  t^3 - 9 t   \cr
y \amp  = \amp  9 t^2 - t^4  
\end{array}</me>
at the points where <m>t = 3</m> and <m>t = - 3</m>.</p>
<p>For <m>t = 3</m>, the tangent line (in form <m>y=mx+b</m>) is</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
<p>For <m>t = - 3</m> , the tangent line is</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-3x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
